---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { APP_NAME, PUBLISHER, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../lib/constants';
---
<Base
  title={`Privacy Policy — ${APP_NAME}`}
  description={`How ${APP_NAME} handles your information. Private by design: no accounts, no ads, no analytics.`}
>
  <article class="container-x py-20 prose-chorder">
    <h1 class="h-display" style="font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 1.4rem + 3.4vw, 3.5rem);">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-muted mt-3">Effective date: November 5, 2026</p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-6 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        {APP_NAME} is published by {PUBLISHER}. This Privacy Policy explains how {APP_NAME}
        handles information when you use the app.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold">Summary</h2>
      <p>
        {APP_NAME} is designed to work on your device. The app does not require an account, does
        not include advertising, does not include analytics, and does not send your imported
        charts, microphone audio, or app library data to {PUBLISHER} servers.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold">Information you provide to the app</h2>
      <p>
        {APP_NAME} lets you import and manage song charts. Depending on how you use the app,
        this may include:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>PDF files, web pages, or Planning Center charts you choose to import.</li>
        <li>Song titles, artists, keys, chords, lyrics, setlists, notes, tags, and edits you create in the app.</li>
        <li>App preferences such as theme choices and display settings.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This information is stored locally on your device so the app can display, search, edit, and
        organize your charts.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold">Microphone access</h2>
      <p>
        {APP_NAME} may request microphone access for the experimental chord detection feature.
      </p>
      <p>
        Microphone audio is processed on your device to estimate chords and beat information.
        {APP_NAME} does not record, save, upload, or share microphone audio with {PUBLISHER}. You
        can deny microphone permission or stop chord detection at any time.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold">On-device processing</h2>
      <p>
        {APP_NAME} uses on-device processing for features such as PDF import, chart parsing
        and editing, Nashville number conversion, transposition, capo display, and chord
        detection.
      </p>
      <p>
        The app does not use these features to transmit your chart contents or audio to {PUBLISHER}.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold">Planning Center Services import</h2>
      <p>
        If you choose to import from Planning Center Services, {APP_NAME} connects to your
        Planning Center account over the internet. You sign in and approve access in your browser
        on Planning Center&rsquo;s own pages; {APP_NAME} does not see or store your password.
      </p>
      <p>
        {APP_NAME} reads the songs, arrangements, plans and PDF attachments your account can
        access, and downloads the charts you choose to import. Planning Center may record that an
        attachment was opened. {APP_NAME} does not edit songs, arrangements or plans in Services.
        Requests go directly from your device to Planning Center, not through {PUBLISHER} servers.
      </p>
      <p>
        The access and refresh tokens that keep you signed in are encrypted with the Android
        Keystore and stored in a private area of the app that is excluded from Android backup.
        Disconnecting in the app clears them from your device. It does not revoke the
        authorization in Planning Center; you can do that from your Planning Center account.
        Charts you imported stay on your device as local copies. Planning Center&rsquo;s own privacy policy governs the
        information it holds.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold">Web-page import</h2>
      <p>
        If you choose to import a chart from a web page, {APP_NAME} requests the address you
        entered directly from your device. The site that hosts the page can see that request, as
        with any web browser. The page is converted into an editable chart on your device and
        saved locally. {PUBLISHER} does not receive the address or the page.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold">Library backup files</h2>
      <p>
        In Settings you can export your library to a file and restore it later. Exporting and
        restoring happen only when you choose them, using Android&rsquo;s file picker, and you
        decide where the file is saved or sent, for example local storage or a cloud document
        provider you have set up. {PUBLISHER} does not receive backup files.
      </p>
      <p>
        A backup contains your saved charts (including edits, keys, capo, metadata and tags),
        notes, annotations, and setlists. It does not contain original PDFs, app settings, or
        Planning Center sign-in details. The file is not encrypted, so anyone who can open it can
        read your charts and notes. Choose where to store or share it accordingly.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold">Information shared with third parties</h2>
      <p>
        {APP_NAME} does not sell your information and does not share your imported charts, app
        library, notes, or microphone audio with third parties. The only network connections the
        app makes are the ones described above: to Planning Center when you use Services import,
        and to a web page when you import from its address.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some app functionality uses Android platform services and libraries on your device, such as
        file picking, local storage, and on-device text recognition. The app can also ask Google
        Play to show its in-app review prompt or open the Play Store listing so you can rate it.
        Your use of Google Play and Android device services is also subject to Google’s privacy
        policies and your device settings.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold">Device backup and transfer</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on your Android device settings, app data may be included in Android backup or
        device-to-device transfer features provided by the operating system. {PUBLISHER} does not
        control those Android backup services.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold">Data retention and deletion</h2>
      <p>
        Your app data remains on your device until you delete it in the app, clear the app’s data,
        uninstall the app, or remove files using Android system tools.
      </p>
      <p>To delete {APP_NAME} data, you can:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>Delete songs, setlists, notes, tags, or imported charts in the app where supported.</li>
        <li>Use Android Settings to clear {APP_NAME}’s app data.</li>
        <li>Uninstall {APP_NAME} from your device.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold">Children’s privacy</h2>
      <p>
        {APP_NAME} is not directed to children under 13. The app does not knowingly collect
        personal information from children.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        {PUBLISHER} may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Updates will be posted with
        a new effective date.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For privacy questions, contact {PUBLISHER} at
        <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
